  "ingredients": [
    "2 tablespoons vegetable oil",
    "4 thick cut pork chops",
    "3 cups day-old bread cubes",
    "0.25 cup butter, melted",
    "0.25 cup chicken broth",
    "2 tablespoons chopped celery",
    "2 tablespoons chopped onion",
    "0.25 teaspoon poultry seasoning",
    "1 (10.5 ounce) can condensed cream of mushroom soup",
    "0.33333334326744 cup water"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather the ingredients. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/qQ35xlhW20VlCV3ITReNq1tf3gw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21140-stuffed-pork-chops-i-ddmfs-4513-4x3-step-01-9b0a462fc7e141c0ab76591159752f93.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21140/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add pork chops and cook until browned, 4 to 6 minutes per side; transfer to a baking dish.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/1ByE9SZw0HeNtGkk9OhW5sFz7lI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21140-stuffed-pork-chops-i-ddmfs-4514-4x3-step-02-01d1bf80aa59455bab331f58dfb8168a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21140/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toss bread cubes, melted butter, chicken broth, celery, onion, and poultry seasoning together in a medium bowl. Spoon heaping mounds of the stuffing mixture onto the pork chops.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/EHZEPe0QpuciOlI7Ed6y0w0nb8k=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21140-stuffed-pork-chops-i-ddmfs-4516-4x3-step-03-75838f06e8ad45599a7c005da4f1efdc.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21140/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine condensed soup with water; pour over the stuffing and pork chops. Cover the baking dish with aluminum foil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/gPTwwplAzOk_csUa1Wm-wsO0RAg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21140-stuffed-pork-chops-i-ddmfs-4517-4x3-step-04-ccd13cdb986940478faff4628a0fd4c3.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21140/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in preheated oven for 30 minutes. Remove foil and continue baking for 10 minutes longer or until juices run clear. A meat thermometer inserted into the center of a pork chop should read 145 degrees F (63 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/SonusJ-LkCc-kgYbuDRILbK1WXQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21140-stuffed-pork-chops-i-ddmfs-4550-4x3-step-05-c71593a48ce741ee8068daa06acff2fd.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21140/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/vTrpKZkqgRcxhclNfxNe9qZovOc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/21140-stuffed-pork-chops-i-ddmfs-4577-4x3-beauty-6344344313c44c7583d84e43d73492d2.jpg"
      ],
